From 5695af68a7379efbaa05a5da9f76bc464debf024 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ohos-kernel-port contributors <232252@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 00:50:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] include: add the missing memcg_policy.h so memcontrol.h can
 be compiled

SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only

Baseline: gitcode.com/openharmony/kernel_linux_6.6
Branch:   OpenHarmony-7.0-Release
Commit:   f4b61510491aa20f7f57fbbc5efc754083c92212
Found by: tools/audit-includes.py

include/linux/memcg_policy.h is not tracked in the repository, and
include/linux/memcontrol.h includes it unconditionally:

    include/linux/memcontrol.h:24:10: fatal error: linux/memcg_policy.h:
        No such file or directory

Four more files include it, all in mm/: memcg_reclaim.c, vmscan.c, zswapd.c and
zswapd_control.c.  memcontrol.h is core and is compiled by every build, so this
is not conditional and cannot be configured away.

Unlike <linux/xpm_types.h>, which has to supply struct definitions because
mm_types.h embeds them by value, nothing here is needed: all four users include
the header and then use no symbol from it, and a tree-wide search finds no
memcg policy definition to supply.  An empty guarded header is the whole fix.

This is the third of the same class in this tree, after the five dangling
Kconfig sources and <linux/xpm_types.h>.  All three are OpenHarmony additions
whose implementations were not published; tools/audit-kconfig.py and
tools/audit-includes.py find them in one pass each so a build does not have to
discover them one at a time.

Upstream: no equivalent; Linux v6.6 has no memcg_policy.h.
Licence: GPL-2.0-only, same as the tree.
---
 include/linux/memcg_policy.h | 29 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 29 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 include/linux/memcg_policy.h

diff --git a/include/linux/memcg_policy.h b/include/linux/memcg_policy.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e0f5175
--- /dev/null
+++ b/include/linux/memcg_policy.h
@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+/* SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only */
+/*
+ * Compatibility shim for the OpenHarmony memcg policy glue.
+ *
+ * include/linux/memcontrol.h includes this header unconditionally, and so do
+ * mm/memcg_reclaim.c, mm/vmscan.c, mm/zswapd.c and mm/zswapd_control.c, but
+ * the file is not tracked in the repository:
+ *
+ *     CC      arch/arm64/kernel/asm-offsets.s
+ *     include/linux/memcontrol.h:24:10: fatal error: linux/memcg_policy.h:
+ *         No such file or directory
+ *
+ * Nothing in this tree declares or defines anything that this header is
+ * supposed to declare: the four users above include it and use no symbol from
+ * it, and a tree-wide search for a memcg policy definition finds nothing.  So
+ * the include is a leftover of a feature whose implementation was not
+ * published, and an empty guarded header is the whole of the fix.
+ *
+ * Unlike <linux/xpm_types.h>, which genuinely needs struct definitions because
+ * mm_types.h embeds them, this one needs nothing — the include resolves and
+ * the build continues.
+ *
+ * When OpenHarmony lands the memcg policy work, delete this file and the
+ * include lines with it.
+ */
+#ifndef _LINUX_MEMCG_POLICY_H
+#define _LINUX_MEMCG_POLICY_H
+
+#endif /* _LINUX_MEMCG_POLICY_H */
-- 
